-- Academy: create Yachts bonus Module 11 as "Bonus: Aurum OS, Your Career Operating System": 28 pages (15 with quick checks, 13 with answerable exercises
-- saved to the Broker Portfolio) + a 10-question final quiz. Same shape as the Module 1 migration.

do $mig$
declare
  v_module uuid;
  v_q uuid;
  v_page uuid;
  rec jsonb;
  n int := 0;
  i int;
  v_pages jsonb := $json$[{"heading": "Bonus: Your Career Operating System", "body": "<p><b>The gap between learning and entering</b></p><p>You have completed ten modules. You understand the yacht, the market, the client, the brokerage business and the career path. You have a portfolio, a target list, an outreach plan and a 30 / 60 / 90-day plan.</p><p>Now comes an uncomfortable truth: <b>knowledge alone does not get anyone into yacht brokerage.</b> People with excellent knowledge stall every day, because the industry is entered through proximity: being visible, informed, consistent and known.</p><p>This bonus module is different. It is not about yachts. It is about <b>the system that carries you through the journey</b>, and why AURUM OS was built as that system. You will tour every part of the platform, use each part on your own journey, and collect evidence of what it does for you. You are not asked to believe anything. You are asked to test it.</p><p>By the end you will understand how AURUM OS supports you from your first day of research to your first year as a broker and beyond, and you will have a personal operating plan for using it.</p>", "q": "What is the purpose of this bonus module?", "opts": ["To teach more yacht terminology", "To show the system that carries you through the journey, and have you test it yourself", "To replace the ten Academy modules", "To ask you to simply trust the platform"], "correct": 1}, {"heading": "Why Career Changers Stall", "body": "<p><b>Five barriers, one operating system</b></p><p>Most people who want to enter a luxury industry are not stopped by intelligence or ambition. They are stopped by five practical barriers:</p><p>&bull; <b>No map:</b> they don't know the sequence. What should I learn first? What should I do this week?<br/>&bull; <b>No proximity:</b> they don't know the people, the events, the news or the language of the room.<br/>&bull; <b>No proof:</b> they cannot show a recruiter or broker anything beyond a CV that says \"keen to learn.\"<br/>&bull; <b>No consistency:</b> they start with energy, then life intervenes and the momentum dies.<br/>&bull; <b>No signal:</b> they cannot tell what matters in the market today, so their outreach sounds generic.</p><p>Each barrier is solved by a different capability, and the problem with most solutions is that they solve <b>one</b> of them. A course gives knowledge but no network. A recruiter gives introductions but no preparation. Social media gives visibility but no structure. A general AI chatbot gives answers but no memory of who you are.</p><p><b>AURUM OS is built around a different idea:</b> one system that addresses all five barriers together, and knows you well enough to keep them connected. The map is your Roadmap and Academy. Proximity is Intelligence, Network and Calendar. Proof is your Broker Portfolio and Content Studio. Consistency is your daily ritual, streak and tasks. Signal is the live Intelligence feed and your Mentor.</p>", "q": "Which barrier does the Broker Portfolio mainly address?", "opts": ["No map", "No consistency", "No signal", "No proof"], "correct": 3}, {"heading": "Exercise: Diagnose Your Own Barriers", "body": "<p><b>Where are you stuck?</b></p><p>Rate each barrier honestly from 1 to 5 (1 = not a problem for me, 5 = a serious problem). Then name the one you most need help with.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Be honest. This decides how you use the rest of the module.", "groups": [{"title": "My five barriers", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "b_map", "label": "No map: I don't know what to do first or this week", "type": "rating"}, {"key": "b_prox", "label": "No proximity: I don't know the people, events, news and language", "type": "rating"}, {"key": "b_proof", "label": "No proof: I can't show anyone real evidence of my ability", "type": "rating"}, {"key": "b_cons", "label": "No consistency: I start well, then momentum fades", "type": "rating"}, {"key": "b_sig", "label": "No signal: I can't tell what matters in the market today", "type": "rating"}]}, {"title": "My biggest barrier", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "b_big", "label": "The barrier that has held me back most, and a real example of it", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "b_past", "label": "What I have tried before to solve it, and why it did or didn't work", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 1: Your Identity and Personalised Setup", "body": "<p><b>The system starts by knowing you</b></p><p>When you join AURUM OS, you don't land in a generic dashboard. You complete a short onboarding of nine questions: which elite ecosystem you are entering, where you stand today, the outcomes you want, how much time you can commit each day, when you have the energy to focus, where you are coming from, where your daily rituals should focus and what is holding you back most. Then it builds your operating system around the answers.</p><p>Your <b>Identity</b> page is your professional dossier. It holds the profile AURUM uses to personalise every recommendation, your connected social accounts and your <b>AURUM Score</b>, an overall measure built from several parts of your activity: profile completeness, core progress, Academy progress, community activity, content published and identity.</p><p><b>Why this matters</b></p><p>Generic advice is easy to find. <b>Personalised</b> advice is rare. Because the system knows your level, goal and time budget, its recommendations for a hospitality manager with one hour a day will differ from those for a former captain with four hours. The industry switcher also means the platform is designed around the luxury world you are entering, starting with yachting, with aviation, automotive and luxury real estate as the wider vision.</p><p>Your preferences stay in your control: you can adjust your active mode, experience level, goal, mentor tone and response style in Settings, export your data and delete your account.</p>", "q": "What is the AURUM Score?", "opts": ["An overall measure built from several parts of your activity and profile", "A grade given by yacht brokerages", "Your Academy quiz average only", "A rating of your social media followers"], "correct": 0}, {"heading": "Exercise: Set Up Your Identity", "body": "<p><b>Make the system yours</b></p><p>Complete your onboarding and identity in AURUM OS, then record what you set.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Do it in the app first, then answer.", "groups": [{"title": "My setup", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "id_mode", "label": "Which ecosystem, level and daily time commitment did I choose?", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "id_goal", "label": "The goal I entered in my profile, in my own words", "type": "long", "min": 30}, {"key": "id_head", "label": "My professional headline as it appears on my Identity page", "type": "short", "min": 15}, {"key": "id_score", "label": "My starting AURUM Score and the part of it I most want to improve", "type": "long", "min": 30}, {"key": "id_tone", "label": "The mentor tone and response style I chose, and why", "type": "long", "min": 30}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 2: The Consistency Engine", "body": "<p><b>Outsider to operator in 30 days</b></p><p>The biggest predictor of career-change success is not talent. It is <b>showing up repeatedly</b>. AURUM OS turns consistency into a system with four connected parts:</p><p>&bull; <b>The 30-day Roadmap:</b> a personalised entry plan built around your industry, level and goals, organised week by week, with specific daily actions you tick off. It is drawn as an actual journey, so you can see your distance travelled.<br/>&bull; <b>The daily ritual:</b> your home base each day, with mode-specific tasks tuned to your time budget and focus, so you never start a session asking \"what should I do?\"<br/>&bull; <b>Per-task AI help:</b> stuck on a task? Tap <b>Get help</b> and receive concrete guidance for that exact task: facts to verify, a step-by-step mini-plan or a short template you can use immediately. No dead ends.<br/>&bull; <b>Streaks, tasks and the Calendar:</b> completions and streaks are recorded on a calendar you can look back on, with tasks, due dates and reminders, so nothing you set out to do slips.</p><p><b>Why this beats willpower</b></p><p>Willpower fades. Systems don't. A visible streak, a calendar of completed work and a task that is already decided for you reduce the friction that ends most career changes in week three. This is the same principle as the weekly scorecard from Module 10, but built into the platform.</p>", "q": "What should you do when you are stuck on a roadmap task?", "opts": ["Skip the task and hope to return later", "Wait until the next week's plan", "Use Get help to receive concrete, task-specific guidance", "Repeat the previous task"], "correct": 2}, {"heading": "Exercise: Run Your First Week", "body": "<p><b>Use the consistency engine</b></p><p>Open your Roadmap and daily ritual. Complete real tasks for at least three days, use Get help once, and record what happened.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Evidence from actually using it.", "groups": [{"title": "My first week", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "cw_tasks", "label": "The tasks I completed (day by day) and how long each took", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "cw_help", "label": "The task where I used Get help, and what the guidance gave me", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "cw_streak", "label": "My streak so far, and what nearly broke it", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "cw_cal", "label": "How I used the Calendar and task reminders to protect my time", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "cw_time", "label": "The best time of day for me to work, based on what I found", "type": "short", "min": 10}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 3: The Academy and Your Personal Tutor", "body": "<p><b>Learn methodically, then prove it</b></p><p>The <b>Academy</b> is a structured curriculum from outsider to fluent. The yacht-broker track you have just completed has ten modules and well over 180 pages of content, with applied exercises rather than passive reading:</p><p>&bull; <b>Reading pages with quick checks</b> to lock in each idea.<br/>&bull; <b>Answerable exercises</b> that you complete in your own words.<br/>&bull; <b>Module quizzes</b> that you must unlock by completing the checkpoints and exercises, so progress is earned, not skipped.<br/>&bull; <b>Progress tracked module by module</b>, with celebrations when you complete a module or track.</p><p><b>The Tutor</b></p><p>Beside the Academy sits the <b>Tutor</b>: step-by-step lessons matched to your exact curriculum, with unlimited follow-up questions and saved lesson history. It is designed to teach from the course content and not to hand out quiz answers. That is deliberate. Its purpose is understanding, not shortcuts.</p><p><b>Why it matters</b></p><p>A recruiter cannot see what you have learned. But they can see <b>what you have produced</b>. That is the next tour.</p>", "q": "Why does the Tutor not simply give you quiz answers?", "opts": ["Because it cannot answer questions", "Because quizzes are optional", "Because answers are hidden from all users forever", "It is designed to build understanding from the course content, not shortcuts"], "correct": 3}, {"heading": "Exercise: Test the Tutor", "body": "<p><b>Put the Tutor to work</b></p><p>Open the Tutor and ask three real questions about a topic you still find difficult.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Use it as a real study partner.", "groups": [{"title": "Three Tutor sessions", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "tu_topic", "label": "The topic I found most difficult in the Academy, and why", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "tu_q1", "label": "Question 1 I asked the Tutor, and the most useful part of its answer", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "tu_q2", "label": "Question 2 (a follow-up that went deeper), and what I learned", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "tu_q3", "label": "Question 3 (something the Academy didn't cover directly), and its answer", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "tu_verdict", "label": "Did the Tutor teach me or just tell me? What would I change?", "type": "long", "min": 40}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 4: Your Broker Portfolio", "body": "<p><b>Proof, assembled automatically</b></p><p>Every answerable exercise you complete in the yacht-broker Academy is saved. The <b>Broker Portfolio</b> gathers those answers into a professional body of work, organised into sections: profile, yachts, sales, market, services and testimonials. You can edit your public profile details (name, headline, location, email, phone, website) and present the work as your own.</p><p>By graduation it contains the pieces you built: your yacht world map, comparisons, market analysis, client brief, recommendation, communication playbook, transferable skills map, target companies, networking database, outreach plan, career entry plan, final broker challenge, 30 / 60 / 90-day plan and first ten opportunities.</p><p><b>Why this is different</b></p><p>Most career changers apply with a CV that says they are enthusiastic. You can say: <b>\"Here is my client brief, my market analysis and my recommendation for a fictional buyer. Here is how I think.\"</b> A hiring broker learns more in five minutes with a portfolio than in an hour of generic conversation. That is the difference between claiming ability and demonstrating it, exactly the principle from Module 9.</p>", "q": "What is the main advantage of the Broker Portfolio?", "opts": ["It replaces the need for a CV entirely", "It demonstrates how you think instead of only claiming enthusiasm", "It guarantees an interview", "It is only useful after you are hired"], "correct": 1}, {"heading": "Exercise: Audit Your Portfolio", "body": "<p><b>Look at it as a hiring broker would</b></p><p>Open your Broker Portfolio and review it critically.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Honest, specific and improvement-focused.", "groups": [{"title": "Portfolio audit", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "pa_strong", "label": "The three strongest pieces in my portfolio, and why", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "pa_weak", "label": "The weakest piece, and how I would improve it", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "pa_profile", "label": "Is my public profile (headline, location, contact details) complete and professional? What did I change?", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "pa_show", "label": "If a broker gave me five minutes, which three sections would I show first, and why?", "type": "long", "min": 60}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 5: The Intelligence Feed", "body": "<p><b>The signal beneath the noise</b></p><p>Brokers are not judged only on what they know. They are judged on how <b>current</b> they are. The <b>Intelligence</b> feed delivers a live stream of curated news and moves in your industry: deals, people, market shifts, events and regulation. It is filtered to your industry and refreshed on a regular cycle, so you see what matters without hunting across dozens of publications.</p><p>&bull; Stories are categorised, so you see only what is relevant.<br/>&bull; Full briefs open without leaving the page.<br/>&bull; <b>One-tap content generation</b> turns any story into a post or talking point.</p><p><b>How a broker uses signal</b></p><p>Read alone, news is entertainment. Used properly, it becomes <b>reasons to speak</b>. A new delivery, a sale, a regulatory change, a refit or a show announcement is a legitimate, specific, timely reason to send a message to a broker or contact: <em>\"I saw the announcement about... and wondered how it affects...\"</em> That converts the generic outreach you were warned about in Module 9 into relevant, personalised outreach. It also gives you the language of the room before you enter it.</p>", "q": "How does the Intelligence feed improve outreach?", "opts": ["It sends messages on your behalf", "It replaces the need for research", "It gives specific, timely reasons to contact people instead of generic messages", "It only lists job advertisements"], "correct": 2}, {"heading": "Exercise: Build a Market Briefing", "body": "<p><b>Turn news into professional value</b></p><p>Open the Intelligence feed and choose three stories relevant to your target companies.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Interpret, don't just summarise.", "groups": [{"title": "Story 1", "section": "market", "fields": [{"key": "mi1_story", "label": "The story (headline and source)", "type": "short", "min": 15}, {"key": "mi1_meaning", "label": "What does it mean for the yacht market?", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "mi1_hook", "label": "An outreach opening I could use because of it", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}, {"title": "Story 2", "section": "market", "fields": [{"key": "mi2_story", "label": "The story (headline and source)", "type": "short", "min": 15}, {"key": "mi2_meaning", "label": "What does it mean for the yacht market?", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "mi2_hook", "label": "An outreach opening I could use because of it", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}, {"title": "Story 3", "section": "market", "fields": [{"key": "mi3_story", "label": "The story (headline and source)", "type": "short", "min": 15}, {"key": "mi3_meaning", "label": "What does it mean for the yacht market?", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "mi3_hook", "label": "An outreach opening I could use because of it", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}, {"title": "My routine", "section": "market", "fields": [{"key": "mi_routine", "label": "How often will I read the feed, and how will I record what I learn?", "type": "long", "min": 40}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 6: Your Mentor, Available Every Day", "body": "<p><b>A strategist who remembers you</b></p><p>The <b>Mentor</b> is an open conversation with AURUM about your career moves, decisions and positioning. It is not a generic chatbot. It understands your industry, level and current focus, keeps your saved conversation history so you can pick up where you left off, and adapts to your streak and goals. It suggests fresh conversation starters based on what is actually happening in your industry now, and on your real progress, rather than a static list.</p><p><b>What a mentor is for across a broker career</b></p><p>&bull; <b>Before outreach:</b> review a message, sharpen the angle or choose whom to contact first.<br/>&bull; <b>Before an interview:</b> rehearse the STAR answers and career-change story from Module 9.<br/>&bull; <b>Before a viewing or negotiation:</b> role-play a sceptical buyer, an anchoring seller or a difficult objection.<br/>&bull; <b>After a setback:</b> analyse a lost deal or silent contact and decide the next action.<br/>&bull; <b>Before an event:</b> plan the week, the introductions and the follow-ups.<br/>&bull; <b>When you are lost:</b> ask what to do next.</p><p>The point is availability and continuity. A human mentor is worth a great deal but is rarely available at 11pm before a first interview, and doesn't remember every previous conversation. AURUM does, and it will keep doing so as your career grows.</p>", "q": "What makes the Mentor different from a generic chatbot?", "opts": ["It knows your industry, level and context and keeps your conversation history", "It only answers factual questions", "It has no memory between sessions", "It replaces all human networking"], "correct": 0}, {"heading": "Exercise: Run Five Mentor Sessions", "body": "<p><b>Practise with the Mentor</b></p><p>Open the Mentor and work through five scenarios from your own journey.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Use real situations, not hypotheticals.", "groups": [{"title": "Five scenarios", "section": "services", "fields": [{"key": "me1", "label": "1. Outreach review: paste a message you wrote and record the feedback you got", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "me2", "label": "2. Interview rehearsal: a hard question I practised, and how my answer improved", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "me3", "label": "3. Role-play: a sceptical buyer or seller I asked the Mentor to play, and what I learned", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "me4", "label": "4. Decision: a career decision I asked about, and the advice I received", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "me5", "label": "5. Next step: what the Mentor suggested I do this week", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "me_verdict", "label": "Where did the Mentor add real value, and where did I need to challenge it?", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 7: Network and Outreach", "body": "<p><b>Yachting is a relationship business</b></p><p>Module 10 asked you to build a 30-person network database. AURUM OS builds it into the platform as the <b>Network</b> page:</p><p>&bull; A <b>contact list organised by category</b>, with yacht-specific categories such as charter broker, sales broker, captain or crew, shipyard, marina, charter management, insurance and survey or refit.<br/>&bull; <b>AI-drafted, personalised outreach</b> for each contact, using your profile and the context you provide, so you start from a strong draft instead of a blank page.<br/>&bull; <b>Sent-message tracking</b>, so nothing falls through the cracks and every follow-up is deliberate.<br/>&bull; A <b>community board</b> to connect with other members, share events and ask questions.</p><p><b>The compounding effect</b></p><p>A spreadsheet stores names. A system <b>works the relationships</b>. When your contacts, drafts, sent messages and follow-ups live next to your Mentor, Intelligence feed and Calendar, every part of the journey feeds the others. A market story becomes a reason to write to a contact. A drafted message becomes a tracked conversation. A follow-up becomes a calendar task. That is the difference between collecting contacts and building a network.</p>", "q": "What is the advantage of managing outreach inside the platform?", "opts": ["It automatically sends unlimited messages", "Contacts, drafts, tracking and follow-ups work together instead of in separate tools", "It removes the need to personalise", "It guarantees replies"], "correct": 1}, {"heading": "Exercise: Load Your Network", "body": "<p><b>Build it in the system</b></p><p>Add your first real contacts to the Network page, draft messages and track what you send.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Real contacts, real messages.", "groups": [{"title": "My network in the system", "section": "services", "fields": [{"key": "nw_add", "label": "How many contacts I added, and the categories they fall into", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "nw_top", "label": "My three most valuable contacts and why", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "nw_draft", "label": "A message I drafted with AI, and how I edited it to sound like me", "type": "long", "min": 80}, {"key": "nw_sent", "label": "Messages sent so far, replies received and the next follow-up dates", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "nw_comm", "label": "One thing I posted, asked or learned on the community board", "type": "long", "min": 30}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 8: Content Studio and Personal Brand", "body": "<p><b>Become known before you are hired</b></p><p>Brokers hire people they have already heard of. <b>Content Studio</b> helps you build professional visibility without needing to be a marketer. It is described as an AI creative director for your industry. It produces:</p><p>&bull; platform-specific captions and hooks<br/>&bull; full scripts with shot-by-shot beats<br/>&bull; hashtag sets tuned to your industry<br/>&bull; AI-assisted visuals<br/>&bull; content grounded in <b>live signals</b> from the Intelligence feed, so it reflects what is happening now</p><p>You can schedule posts, see them on your Calendar, and connect accounts such as LinkedIn to share.</p><p><b>Using it wisely</b></p><p>Content Studio is a drafting tool, not a substitute for judgment. The best use for a career changer is a modest, consistent, professional presence: sharing what you are learning, a considered view on a market story or a lesson from a deal scenario. Never claim experience you do not have, and never publish confidential information. Your credibility is built on accuracy, which is the same integrity principle as the Final Broker Challenge.</p>", "q": "What is the wise way to use Content Studio as a career changer?", "opts": ["Post constantly to appear experienced", "Exaggerate your background to stand out", "Copy other brokers' posts", "A modest, consistent, honest presence that never claims experience you lack"], "correct": 3}, {"heading": "Exercise: Draft Your Professional Voice", "body": "<p><b>Build a credible presence</b></p><p>Use Content Studio to draft and refine one professional post.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Honest, useful and appropriate.", "groups": [{"title": "My first professional post", "section": "services", "fields": [{"key": "cs_topic", "label": "The topic, the story it was based on and the audience", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "cs_draft", "label": "The post I published or scheduled (final version)", "type": "long", "min": 200}, {"key": "cs_edit", "label": "What I changed from the AI draft to make it accurate and personal", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "cs_plan", "label": "My content rhythm: how often, on which platform, and about what for the next 30 days", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "cs_rules", "label": "My own rules for content: what I will and won't say", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}]}}, {"heading": "Tour 9: Events, Calendar and the Room", "body": "<p><b>Know where to be</b></p><p>Yachting is a seasonal, event-driven industry. The Monaco Yacht Show, the Cannes Yachting Festival, the Fort Lauderdale Boat Show and others are where brokers, captains, owners' representatives and shipyards gather. Being present, prepared and known at these events is a career accelerator.</p><p>AURUM OS lays industry events on the same <b>Calendar</b> as your rituals, tasks, reminders and scheduled posts, along with events shared by community members, so your preparation windows are visible: research, outreach before the show, meetings during and follow-up after.</p><p><b>The event cycle</b></p><p>&bull; <b>Six weeks before:</b> research attendees, book meetings, draft outreach.<br/>&bull; <b>During:</b> observe, listen, ask good questions and log every conversation.<br/>&bull; <b>After:</b> follow up within days, using the specific context of each conversation.</p><p>A calendar that connects preparation, presence and follow-up turns a costly trip into a structured opportunity.</p>", "q": "What should happen after an industry event?", "opts": ["Prompt, specific follow-up using the context of each conversation", "Nothing; the event is the goal", "Send the same generic message to everyone", "Wait a year and reintroduce yourself"], "correct": 0}, {"heading": "Exercise: Plan Your First Event", "body": "<p><b>Turn an event into a plan</b></p><p>Choose one real industry event and plan it in your Calendar.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Preparation, presence and follow-up.", "groups": [{"title": "My event plan", "section": "market", "fields": [{"key": "ev_which", "label": "The event, date, location and why it is relevant to me", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "ev_pre", "label": "Before: research, outreach and meetings I will arrange, with dates", "type": "long", "min": 70}, {"key": "ev_during", "label": "During: who I will speak to, what I will ask, how I will record it", "type": "long", "min": 70}, {"key": "ev_post", "label": "After: my follow-up plan for the first 7 days", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "ev_cal", "label": "How I set this up in my Calendar (tasks, reminders, scheduled posts)", "type": "long", "min": 40}]}]}}, {"heading": "The Whole Journey: Aurum OS at Every Stage", "body": "<p><b>Beside you for the entire career</b></p><p>AURUM OS is not only an entry tool. It is designed to remain useful as your role changes:</p><p>&bull; <b>Days 1 to 30, foundation:</b> onboarding, Roadmap and the Academy build your map and knowledge. Tutor and Mentor answer questions. Portfolio begins to fill.<br/>&bull; <b>Days 31 to 90, entering the room:</b> Intelligence gives you reasons to speak. Network tracks outreach. Studio builds visibility. Calendar prepares you for events. Mentor rehearses interviews.<br/>&bull; <b>First role:</b> the same Mentor helps you plan your first viewings, difficult conversations and negotiations. The Academy modules remain a reference library. Intelligence keeps you current on the market you now work in.<br/>&bull; <b>First year:</b> Network becomes your client and contact relationship tool. Studio supports your professional brand. Your streak and score become a record of professional discipline.<br/>&bull; <b>Senior broker:</b> as your reputation grows, the system still helps you monitor the market, maintain relationships and communicate with authority.</p><p><b>Why continuity is the real value</b></p><p>Most tools serve one moment: a course ends, a recruiter moves on, a chatbot forgets. AURUM OS keeps the context of who you are, what you have done and what you are aiming for. The longer you use it, the more relevant it becomes, because the profile, history and network it draws on are yours. That compounding continuity is something a one-off course cannot replicate.</p>", "q": "Why does long-term use make the platform more valuable?", "opts": ["Because the price falls over time", "Because it gives you a job title", "Your profile, history and network build up, so its guidance becomes more relevant", "Because you no longer need to make decisions"], "correct": 2}, {"heading": "Exercise: Design Your Weekly Operating Rhythm", "body": "<p><b>Make the system a habit</b></p><p>Design how you will use AURUM OS in a typical week during your job search.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Specific days, tools and outcomes.", "groups": [{"title": "My weekly rhythm", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "wr_mon", "label": "Monday: which tools I use and what I produce", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "wr_tue", "label": "Tuesday", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "wr_wed", "label": "Wednesday", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "wr_thu", "label": "Thursday", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "wr_fri", "label": "Friday: my weekly review and scorecard", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "wr_weekend", "label": "Weekend: lighter learning, reflection or event preparation", "type": "long", "min": 30}, {"key": "wr_metric", "label": "The three measures I will track to know whether it is working", "type": "long", "min": 50}]}]}}, {"heading": "Under the Hood: Built to Be Trusted", "body": "<p><b>Why the foundations matter</b></p><p>You are entrusting a career change to a platform, so it is fair to ask how it is built. In plain language:</p><p>&bull; <b>Your data is protected.</b> Each user's data sits behind database-level security rules, so accounts can only access their own records. You can export your data or delete your account from Settings.<br/>&bull; <b>Quizzes are honest.</b> Answers are graded on the server, not revealed in the browser, so passing a module means something.<br/>&bull; <b>Premium actions are protected.</b> Server functions for image generation, posting and payments require authenticated users, and payment webhooks verify signatures before acting.<br/>&bull; <b>The intelligence feed is real.</b> It is fed by an automated pipeline that gathers and categorises live industry news into a database on a regular cycle, not a static demo.<br/>&bull; <b>The AI is abstracted.</b> The platform is designed so the underlying AI provider can change without rebuilding the product, which protects it against any single supplier.<br/>&bull; <b>It speaks your language.</b> The interface supports English and French.<br/>&bull; <b>It is built for growth.</b> A modern web stack and a managed database allow it to scale, and the same architecture supports additional industries beyond yachting.</p><p><b>Honest limits</b></p><p>No platform can promise a job. AURUM OS improves your preparation, visibility and consistency. You must still do the work, and outcomes depend on the market and your effort. A system that respects that is more credible than one that promises otherwise.</p>", "q": "What can no platform honestly promise you?", "opts": ["Better preparation", "More consistent activity", "A structured plan", "A guaranteed job"], "correct": 3}, {"heading": "The Proof: Aurum OS Against the Alternatives", "body": "<p><b>Compare honestly</b></p><p>Consider the ways people commonly try to enter a luxury industry, and what each does well:</p><p>&bull; <b>Courses and books:</b> excellent for knowledge. Usually they don't give a daily plan, live market signal, contact tracking or a memory of you.<br/>&bull; <b>Recruiters:</b> valuable for introductions once you are ready. They don't teach you, prepare you or work on your schedule.<br/>&bull; <b>Social media and networking sites:</b> great for visibility. They provide no structure, no curriculum and a lot of noise.<br/>&bull; <b>General AI chatbots:</b> useful for answers. They don't know your industry context, hold a persistent profile, track your streak or link to your contacts and calendar.<br/>&bull; <b>Going alone:</b> flexible, but the five barriers all remain unsolved.</p><p><b>AURUM OS combines the strengths in one system:</b> a structured curriculum, a personal plan, live market signal, an AI mentor and tutor with context, a network tool, a content studio, a calendar and a portfolio that turns your learning into evidence.</p><p><b>The strongest proof is your own</b></p><p>This module does not ask you to accept these claims. You have used the Roadmap, Tutor, Portfolio, Intelligence, Mentor, Network, Studio and Calendar. The proof is what you produced. The next exercise makes it explicit.</p>", "q": "What is the strongest proof of the platform's value?", "opts": ["Claims made in marketing", "What you personally produced and achieved using it", "The number of features listed", "Other people's opinions alone"], "correct": 1}, {"heading": "Exercise: The Proof Test", "body": "<p><b>Prove it to yourself</b></p><p>Look at the evidence honestly. What did AURUM OS change for you?</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "Evidence, not enthusiasm. Include what did not work.", "groups": [{"title": "Before and after", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "pt_before", "label": "Where I stood on my five barriers before (refer to your first exercise)", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "pt_after", "label": "Where I stand now, and what evidence shows the change", "type": "long", "min": 80}, {"key": "pt_best", "label": "The single feature that helped me most, and a specific result it produced", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "pt_weak", "label": "The feature that helped least, or what I would improve in the platform", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "pt_alt", "label": "What I would have done differently or slower without a system like this", "type": "long", "min": 60}]}]}}, {"heading": "Professional Output: My Aurum OS Operating Plan", "body": "<p><b>My Aurum OS Operating Plan</b></p><p>A one-page plan for using the platform over the next 90 days. It becomes part of your Broker Portfolio and shows how systematically you approach the career.</p>", "exercise": {"intro": "One page. Specific, measurable and yours.", "groups": [{"title": "Page 1: My operating plan", "section": "profile", "fields": [{"key": "op_goal", "label": "My 90-day goal and the role I am pursuing", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "op_daily", "label": "My daily minimum (ritual, streak, learning)", "type": "long", "min": 40}, {"key": "op_weekly", "label": "My weekly targets (outreach, follow-ups, conversations, content)", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "op_tools", "label": "The three AURUM OS tools I will rely on most, and for what", "type": "long", "min": 60}, {"key": "op_review", "label": "How and when I will review progress and change the plan", "type": "long", "min": 50}, {"key": "op_stat", "label": "The first thing I will do in AURUM OS tomorrow", "type": "long", "min": 30}]}]}}, {"heading": "Final Reflection: The Journey Continues", "body": "<p><b>The Academy ends. The system doesn't.</b></p><p>You began this Academy asking whether you could build a career in yachting. You now have knowledge, a portfolio, a plan and a system that keeps working beside you.</p><p>AURUM OS is not a shortcut. It is a structure for doing the work that gets people in: learning methodically, staying informed, building relationships, creating proof, showing up consistently and adapting the strategy from evidence.</p><p>Yachting is the first world it serves. The same approach is planned for aviation, automotive and luxury real estate, so the discipline you have learned here becomes a repeatable method for entering elite industries.</p><p><b>Your next step:</b> open your Roadmap, complete today's ritual and send one personalised message. Then do it again tomorrow. That is how careers are built.</p>", "q": "According to the final reflection, what is AURUM OS?", "opts": ["A guaranteed route to a job", "A replacement for human relationships", "A structure for doing the work that gets people in, not a shortcut", "A one-time course"], "correct": 2}]$json$;
  v_final jsonb := $json$[{"q": "Why do career changers commonly stall, according to this module?", "opts": ["They lack intelligence", "They face practical barriers such as no map, no proximity, no proof, no consistency and no signal", "They start too late in life", "Yachting is closed to newcomers"], "correct": 1}, {"q": "What does the Broker Portfolio provide that a CV alone does not?", "opts": ["A guaranteed interview", "A replacement for experience", "Automatic job applications", "Evidence of how you think, through the work you produced"], "correct": 3}, {"q": "How does the Intelligence feed help your outreach?", "opts": ["It supplies timely, specific reasons to contact people", "It sends messages for you", "It removes the need to research", "It lists only vacancies"], "correct": 0}, {"q": "What makes the Mentor different from a generic chatbot?", "opts": ["It never gives advice", "It only works once", "It knows your industry, level and context and keeps your history", "It replaces every human mentor"], "correct": 2}, {"q": "What is the sensible use of Content Studio for a career changer?", "opts": ["Publishing as often as possible", "Claiming experience to seem credible", "Sharing confidential information", "A modest, consistent, honest presence that never overstates experience"], "correct": 3}, {"q": "Why does the Network tool add more value than a spreadsheet?", "opts": ["It guarantees replies", "Contacts, drafts, tracking and follow-ups work alongside the rest of the platform", "It writes messages you never review", "It removes the need for personalisation"], "correct": 1}, {"q": "How should an industry event be treated in your plan?", "opts": ["As preparation before, structured presence during and prompt follow-up after", "As a place to hand out your CV", "As a social outing only", "As something to attend without research"], "correct": 0}, {"q": "Why does continuity matter over a whole career?", "opts": ["It makes decisions for you", "It lets you skip learning", "The system keeps your context, so its guidance becomes more relevant over time", "It guarantees promotion"], "correct": 2}, {"q": "What can AURUM OS honestly not promise?", "opts": ["Structured preparation", "A guaranteed job", "Consistent activity tracking", "Access to a personal mentor"], "correct": 1}, {"q": "What is the strongest proof of the platform's value to you?", "opts": ["Marketing claims", "The length of its feature list", "Testimonials alone", "The evidence of what you produced and changed by using it"], "correct": 3}]$json$;
begin
  insert into public.academy_modules (track, phase_number, phase_title, module_number, title, description)
  select 'yachts', 5, 'BONUS', 11, 'Bonus: Aurum OS, Your Career Operating System', 'How Aurum OS carries you from first research to a long broker career.'
  where not exists (select 1 from public.academy_modules where track = 'yachts' and module_number = 11);
  select id into v_module from public.academy_modules where track = 'yachts' and module_number = 11;
  if v_module is null then
    raise exception 'Yachts module 11 not found';
  end if;

  update public.academy_modules
     set title = 'Bonus: Aurum OS, Your Career Operating System', description = 'How Aurum OS carries you from first research to a long broker career.'
   where id = v_module;

  delete from public.academy_module_pages where module_id = v_module;
  delete from public.academy_quiz_questions where module_id = v_module;

  for rec in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_pages) loop
    n := n + 1;
    if rec ? 'exercise' then
      insert into public.academy_module_pages (module_id, page_number, heading, body_html, checkpoint_question_id, exercise)
      values (v_module, n, rec->>'heading', rec->>'body', null, rec->'exercise');
    else
      insert into public.academy_quiz_questions (module_id, question_text, order_index, stage, page_number)
      values (v_module, rec->>'q', 0, 'checkpoint', n)
      returning id into v_q;

      for i in 0 .. jsonb_array_length(rec->'opts') - 1 loop
        insert into public.academy_quiz_options (question_id, option_text, is_correct, order_index)
        values (v_q, rec->'opts'->>i, i = (rec->>'correct')::int, i);
      end loop;

      insert into public.academy_module_pages (module_id, page_number, heading, body_html, checkpoint_question_id)
      values (v_module, n, rec->>'heading', rec->>'body', v_q);
    end if;
  end loop;

  n := 0;
  for rec in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_final) loop
    n := n + 1;
    insert into public.academy_quiz_questions (module_id, question_text, order_index, stage)
    values (v_module, rec->>'q', n - 1, 'final')
    returning id into v_q;

    for i in 0 .. jsonb_array_length(rec->'opts') - 1 loop
      insert into public.academy_quiz_options (question_id, option_text, is_correct, order_index)
      values (v_q, rec->'opts'->>i, i = (rec->>'correct')::int, i);
    end loop;
  end loop;
end
$mig$;
